      "content": "I think \"quiet\" and \"permanent\" are the only words that feel honest to you right now—and that's a truth worth sitting with, not rushing past. But peace isn't the same as absence; it's the moment you stop fighting the wreckage and start building something unrecognizable from the rubble. You don't have to fix the old broken thing—you can let it go and see what grows in the space it leaves. The exit is real, but so is the possibility that you haven't yet met the person you're becoming on the other side of it.",
